een fields when GNU ls only uses one, so I need to adjust the spacing to match the standard output more closely. Fixing the format string to match GNU ls output...\n\nI need to account for the variable widths of the owner and group columns, then right-align the size with appropriate spacing before it. Looking at actual ls output, the spacing between columns depends on the maximum width of each field, so I'm adjusting the format specifiers to handle left-aligned padded fields for owner and group, then a right-aligned size column. I'm realizing the spacing pattern depends on field alignment—the nlink is right-aligned with padding, while owner and group are left-padded to their maximum widths, and size is right-aligned with variable spacing before it based on its width. Let me just implement this format and move forward since the key insight is understanding how each field's alignment creates the spacing. I need to verify the exact spacing by checking how the format string with field widths actually produces output—when owner is left-aligned with padding, that creates the space before group, and I need to make sure size is right-aligned to match GNU ls behavior. I see the issue now—my format string has double spaces between fields when it should only have single spaces like GNU ls does. Let me update the format string to use single space separators instead.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":129525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3986247-14f1-40ab-8591-8e0beb64d116","uuid":"58dfc5d1-6866-4006-96a8-2663f38b4e6d"}
